```

Name the tenant in the message (`plan.tenant.name`, never the GUID, per the UX rules) and offer no override — there is no legitimate reason to graft one tenant's plan onto another. Add a test that a plan file whose `tenant.id` differs leaves the store untouched. While there, apply the same check to `plan.checkpoints`, which is the field that produces the fabricated "deleted" lines.

