findings.fix:
Read the challenge and feed it back through the gate. In `graphRequest`, capture it before retrying:

```ts
if (res && res.status === 401 && count401 < 2) {
  count401 += 1
  const claims = parseClaimsChallenge(res.headers.get('WWW-Authenticate'))
  await tokens.refresh(claims)   // widen TokenSource.refresh to accept an optional claims string
  continue
}
```

Thread `claims` through the worker's `token-needed` message and `runScan.ts`'s gate into `getGraphToken`, and pass it to `acquireTokenSilent({ scopes, account, claims })` — MSAL treats a claims request as a cache miss, so it goes to the STS and, when interaction is required, raises `InteractionRequiredAuthError`, which the existing `'popup'` path at msal.ts:66 already handles by pausing the scan and resuming it. That turns a confusing multi-section failure into the pause the design already specifies.
